# 🛠️ Network Troubleshooting Commands

The following commands can be used when investigating a shared-folder issue.

## Check IP configuration

```cmd
ipconfig /all
```

Purpose:

Displays network configuration including:

* IP address
* Subnet mask
* Default gateway
* DNS server
* DHCP information

---

## Test SERVER01 connectivity

```cmd
ping SERVER01
```

Purpose:

Tests network connectivity and name resolution to the server.

---

## Test SMB port

```powershell
Test-NetConnection SERVER01 -Port 445
```

Purpose:

Tests whether TCP port 445 is reachable on SERVER01.

A successful result should show:

```text
TcpTestSucceeded : True
```

