# 🔐 Why Security Groups Are Used

Instead of assigning permissions individually to each user, permissions can be assigned to a security group.

Example:

```text
50 Finance users
       ↓
  GG-Finance
       ↓
Finance folder
```

When a new employee joins Finance:

```text
Create account
      ↓
Add user to GG-Finance
      ↓
User receives authorized access
```

When the employee leaves Finance:

```text
Remove user from GG-Finance
      ↓
Finance access removed
```

This makes access management easier to maintain.

