# 🔑 NTFS Permissions

NTFS permissions control access to files and folders on the Windows filesystem.

For the Finance folder:

```text
C:\Shares\Finance
```

the Finance security group can be assigned appropriate NTFS permissions.

Example lab configuration:

```text
GG-Finance
    ↓
Modify
```

Modify permissions allow authorized users to work with files without automatically giving them Full Control.

---

# 🌐 Share Permissions

Share permissions control access when a folder is accessed through the network share.

The two major permission layers are:

```text
Share Permissions
        +
NTFS Permissions
        ↓
Effective Access
```

This means that troubleshooting a shared-folder problem requires examining both permission layers.

---

# 🧠 Share vs NTFS

## Share Permissions

Control:

```text
Network access
```

Example:

```text
\\SERVER01\Finance
```

## NTFS Permissions

Control:

```text
Filesystem access
```

Example:

```text
C:\Shares\Finance
```

For network access:

```text
Share
+
NTFS
↓
Effective access
```

