# 🧠 Troubleshooting Principle

A useful troubleshooting principle reinforced today was:

> **Test the actual resource directly before assuming that the resource is unavailable.**

For example:

```text
Network view doesn't show SERVER01
            ↓
Don't immediately conclude:
"Server is down."
            ↓
Try:
\\SERVER01\Finance
            ↓
Share opens
            ↓
Server/share is reachable
```

---

# 🛡️ Security Principle

Do not solve a permission problem by giving broad permissions such as:

```text
Everyone
↓
Full Control
```

Instead:

```text
Identify required access
        ↓
Verify authorization
        ↓
Use appropriate security group
        ↓
Assign minimum necessary permission
        ↓
Verify access
```

This applies the principle of **least privilege**.

